    "body": "In case the external SD card is formatted as mobile / removable storage (FAT32) and not as encrypted/bound to the device, the SD card can be removed and read out by any attacker, thief, or finder of a device.\r\n\r\nThe unencrypted, XML-style Osmand profile data easily reveals the saved and used locations of the device owner: home and work location, favourite places, tracks, and potentially even data of related people. This is like address badges on your keys and not compatible with EU privacy law (GDPR).\r\n\r\nSo, Osmand should retain privacy-related profile data (locations history favourite places, home and work locations, settings, GPX tracks, navigation settings and cache) separate from large \"bulk\" data (maps, sounds, fonts, ...) and keep privacy-related information in internal storage and/or let the user choose where to save profile and map / bulk data independently.\r\n",
